{"page":250,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.04911,"w":0.29692,"h":0.01851,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"236 Chapter 4: Applications of Derivatives"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09056,"w":0.18995,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"By substituting, we conclude"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.11295,"w":0.36629,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"ln bx = ln b + ln x.\b"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.13064,"w":0.58893,"h":0.03558,"fs":0.01311,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Proof that ln x r = r ln x We use the same-derivative argument again. For all posi- tive values of x,"},{"x":0.43736,"y":0.17689,"w":0.06527,"h":0.02363,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ln xr = 1"},{"x":0.4218,"y":0.17691,"w":0.01551,"h":0.02855,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dx"},{"x":0.49257,"y":0.17691,"w":0.02807,"h":0.02812,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"xr d"},{"x":0.52432,"y":0.18325,"w":0.17928,"h":0.01494,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"(xr) Chain Rule"},{"x":0.50884,"y":0.1914,"w":0.01543,"h":0.01407,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx"},{"x":0.46813,"y":0.21142,"w":0.0345,"h":0.02363,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= 1"},{"x":0.49257,"y":0.21722,"w":0.27021,"h":0.02234,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"xr rxr-1 Derivative Power Rule"},{"x":0.46813,"y":0.2431,"w":0.04991,"h":0.02904,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= r # 1"},{"x":0.51033,"y":0.24597,"w":0.04401,"h":0.02786,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x = d"},{"x":0.55801,"y":0.25298,"w":0.05361,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(r ln x)."},{"x":0.54254,"y":0.26046,"w":0.01543,"h":0.01407,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.283,"w":0.30563,"h":0.01494,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Since ln xr and r ln x have the same derivative,"},{"x":0.55621,"y":0.30159,"w":0.12274,"h":0.0217,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ln xr = r ln x + C"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.32971,"w":0.4902,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"for some constant C. Taking x to be 1 identifies C as zero, and we’re done.\b"},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.36041,"w":0.37094,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"You are asked to prove the Quotient Rule for logarithms,"},{"x":0.54487,"y":0.36486,"w":0.03355,"h":0.06906,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ln ab"},{"x":0.57071,"y":0.36486,"w":0.11998,"h":0.06906,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"xb = ln b - ln x,"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.39555,"w":0.59297,"h":0.06906,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"in Exercise 75. The Reciprocal Rule, ln (1>x) = -ln x, is a special case of the Quotient Rule, obtained by taking b = 1 and noting that ln 1 = 0."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.47484,"w":0.14262,"h":0.01658,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Laws of Exponents"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.49914,"w":0.59305,"h":0.03029,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The laws of exponents for the natural exponential ex are consequences of the algebraic properties of ln x. They follow from the inverse relationship between these functions."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.57717,"w":0.17489,"h":0.01527,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Laws of Exponents for ex"},{"x":0.35358,"y":0.59668,"w":0.53251,"h":0.03029,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"For all numbers x, x1, and x2, the natural exponential ex obeys the following laws:"},{"x":0.35358,"y":0.63095,"w":0.2829,"h":0.03099,"fs":0.01918,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"1. ex1 # ex2 = ex1+x2 2. e-x = 1 ex"},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.66749,"w":0.37146,"h":0.02898,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"3. ex1 ex2 = ex1-x2 4. (ex1)x2 = ex1x2 = (ex2)x1"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.7307,"w":0.1452,"h":0.01581,"fs":0.01311,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Proof of Law 1 Let"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.75437,"w":0.58894,"h":0.01983,"fs":0.02542,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"y1 = ex1 and y2 = ex2. (4)"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.77806,"w":0.03362,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Then"},{"x":0.39121,"y":0.79749,"w":0.35097,"h":0.04193,"fs":0.02542,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"x1 = ln y1 and x2 = ln y2 Take logs of both sides of Eqs. (4). x1 + x2 = ln y1 + ln y2"},{"x":0.44062,"y":0.83882,"w":0.35394,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"= ln y1 y2 Product Rule for logarithms"},{"x":0.40656,"y":0.85527,"w":0.3139,"h":0.05833,"fs":0.01279,"n":8,"k":0,"t":"ex1+x2 = eln y1 y2 Exponentiate. = y1 y2 eln u = u = ex1ex2. \b"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.92002,"w":0.56472,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The proof of Law 4 is similar. Laws 2 and 3 follow from Law 1 (Exercises 77 and 78)."}]}